\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Matched-dose ($VK^{2}\approx 36$) numerics for the kinetic completion (Remark\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {rem:numerics}(d)--(e)). (a)\nobreakspace  {}Eigenstate fluctuation ratio $\sigma _{\mathrm  {ETH}}/\mathrm  {std}(a)$ versus truncation dimension: window values (filled) and exact full-spectrum values (open); no decay across a factor $17.6$ in $D$. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Distance of the diagonal ensemble from the microcanonical value, normalized by $K$: $O(1)$ gaps with no closing trend; the $T\leq 22.5$ estimate (cross) is a transient that coincides with the microcanonical value. (c)\nobreakspace  {}The $d=4$, $K=11$, $D=20736$, $V=0.3$ trajectory extended to $\tau =300$: observable, running time average, nested late-time averages (diagonal-ensemble estimate $\approx 4.40$), microcanonical line, and the early transient. (d)\nobreakspace  {}Finite-$T$ plateau versus exact diagonal ensemble at $D\leq 10^{4}$ (identity line).}}{23}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ladder}{{3}{23}{Matched-dose ($VK^{2}\approx 36$) numerics for the kinetic completion (Remark~\ref {rem:numerics}(d)--(e)). (a)~Eigenstate fluctuation ratio $\sigma _{\mathrm {ETH}}/\mathrm {std}(a)$ versus truncation dimension: window values (filled) and exact full-spectrum values (open); no decay across a factor $17.6$ in $D$. (b)~Distance of the diagonal ensemble from the microcanonical value, normalized by $K$: $O(1)$ gaps with no closing trend; the $T\leq 22.5$ estimate (cross) is a transient that coincides with the microcanonical value. (c)~The $d=4$, $K=11$, $D=20736$, $V=0.3$ trajectory extended to $\tau =300$: observable, running time average, nested late-time averages (diagonal-ensemble estimate $\approx 4.40$), microcanonical line, and the early transient. (d)~Finite-$T$ plateau versus exact diagonal ensemble at $D\leq 10^{4}$ (identity line)}{figure.3}{}}
